# SPA routing — React Router owns the URLs, so every path that is not a real
# file must be served index.html. Status 200 (not 301) keeps the URL the
# visitor typed.
#
# This duplicates the redirect in netlify.toml on purpose. netlify.toml lives
# at the repository root and is NOT copied into dist/, so a site deployed by
# dragging the dist folder onto Netlify has no redirect rule at all and every
# route except the homepage 404s. This file ships inside dist/, so routing
# survives either way. Netlify processes netlify.toml rules first and these
# second; the two being identical means no conflict.
/*  /index.html  200
